# Stagepass PHP

Plain PHP 8.2 or newer. No framework, no Composer, no mail. The agent guide is `AGENTS.stagepass.md` (section PHP). Longer notes: [https://stagepass.one/docs/php/](https://stagepass.one/docs/php/).

`api/action.php` is the only public entry. Register actions in `api/actions.php`. Handlers live in `api/actions/`.

## Setup

Copy `api/.env.example` to `.env` in the project root (the folder that contains `api/`). Set `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` to exact origins, including `https://{{NAME}}.sp`. Do not commit `.env`.

That folder is the document root locally, and `dist/` after `stagepass build`. From Webflow, `window.location.origin` is the Webflow host and does not run PHP. Call the PHP host with its absolute URL, for example `https://php.example.com/api/action.php`.

Prefer `stagepass dev` or the linked `.sp` domain. `php -S 127.0.0.1:8080 -t .` matches `/api/action.php` but does not hide `/.env`. Do not point it at a folder that already contains a real `.env`.

Apache uses the project `.htaccess`. nginx does not. Put this in the server block before `location ~ \.php$`:

```nginx
location ~* /\.(?!well-known\/) {
    deny all;
}
```

## New action

The recipe in `AGENTS.stagepass.md` is three steps:

1. Add `api/actions/<name>.php` that returns a callable. Validate with `validate_required`, `validate_email`, and `validate_max_length`. Call another service with curl and a timeout. Read secrets with `env_string` and no default. Log upstream failures with `error_log` and answer with `respond_error`.
2. Register the name in `action_catalog()` (`methods`, `honeypot`, `rate_limit`, `origin`).
3. Call `/api/action.php` with `action` set to that name. Do not add another public `.php` file next to `action.php`.
